function SearchResults({ items, query }) {
  analytics.track("impression", { query }); // fires the tracker
  return <ul>{items.map((i) => <li key={i.id}>{i.title}</li>)}</ul>;
}

Metrics: impressions +40% WoW, traffic flat, page views flat.
Timeline: spike starts the day startTransition shipped.
The tracker call executes during the ___b1___ phase, so it also fires for renders that React ___b2___ when a more urgent update arrives. The fix is to move the call into ___b3___ keyed on query.

